{"duration": 31.1, "timeline": [[0.0, "You might assume cranes were needed to lift a massive stone capstone onto the 208-foot tower, but how did Chola builders succeed in 1010 AD?"], [9.1, "Myths claim levitation or magic."], [11.8, "Others assume multiple smaller blocks."], [14.17, "Both guesses are entirely false."], [16.53, "Scholars propose immense inclined ramps."], [19.43, "Artisans rolled the solid monolith."], [22.07, "Hauling it up sixteen storeys."], [24.03, "Without modern steel or engines."], [26.6, "Pure Chola craftsmanship triumphed."], [28.87, "Yet looking up today..."]]}